## Execution Plan
Follow this plan step by step:
1. Define the `ContentCard` interface in `src/interface/content/contentCard.ts` with fields: `uid: string`, `title: string`, `url: string`, `body?: string`, `metadata?: Record<string, unknown>`, and a `LivePreviewConfig` type containing `host`, `stackId`, `previewToken`, and `livePreview` boolean.

2. Create `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx` exporting a `ContentstackProvider` component and `useContentstackContext` hook. The provider accepts props `{ children: ReactNode; previewConfig?: LivePreviewConfig }` and exposes `{ previewConfig, isPreviewMode, setPreviewMode }` via context. Initialize `isPreviewMode` from URL search params (`?live_preview=true`).

3. In `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx`, add a `useEffect` that registers a `message` event listener on `window` to receive postMessage events from the CMS preview iframe, updating `isPreviewMode` and storing the latest preview entry UID in a `ref`.

4. Create `src/hooks/useContent.ts` exporting a `useContent` hook with signature `useContent<T extends ContentCard>(contentTypeUid: string, entryUid: string): { data: T | null; isLoading: boolean; error: Error | null }`. The hook consumes `useContentstackContext` and appends live-preview query parameters (`live_preview`, `preview_timestamp`, `authtoken`) to the Contentstack SDK query when `isPreviewMode` is true.

5. In `src/hooks/useContent.ts`, implement a `useEffect` that re-fetches content whenever `isPreviewMode` toggles or a preview postMessage is received, using the Contentstack SDK `Stack.ContentType(uid).Entry(uid).fetch()` with conditional live-preview headers.

6. Modify `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx` to accept props `{ href: string; children: ReactNode; className?: string }` and consume `useContentstackContext`. When `isPreviewMode` is true, render the `<a>` tag with `data-cs-preview-uid` and `data-cs-preview-content-type` attributes so the CMS can highlight the linked entry in the preview pane.

7. In `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx`, add an `onClick` handler that, when `isPreviewMode` is true, calls `event.preventDefault()` and `window.parent.postMessage({ action: 'cs-preview-navigate', href }, '*')` to notify the CMS iframe of navigation.

8. Write unit tests for `src/hooks/useContent.ts` mocking the Contentstack SDK and verifying: (a) standard fetch without preview params when `isPreviewMode` is false, (b) fetch includes `live_preview` and `authtoken` params when `isPreviewMode` is true, (c) re-fetch is triggered on postMessage preview events.

9. Write unit tests for `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx` verifying: (a) `isPreviewMode` initializes from `?live_preview=true` URL param, (b) postMessage listener updates preview state, (c) `useContentstackContext` throws when used outside the provider.

10. Write unit tests for `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx` verifying: (a) preview data attributes are present when `isPreviewMode` is true and absent when false, (b) `onClick` prevents default and posts a navigation message to `window.parent` only in preview mode.
